=== Prompt for SKY-004-B (attempt 1) ===
Implement user story SKY-004-B: Search and cheapest API routes with full input validation and complete test suite

## Story Description
Implement GET /search and GET /cheapest in src/server.ts, importing FlightResult from the SKY-002 export. Add all input validation (required params, adults range, date format regex). Expand src/server.test.ts to at least 8 total tests with SkyscannerClient fully mocked. **Depends on SKY-002 and SKY-004-A.**

## Acceptance Criteria
- GET /search with valid query params (from, to, date, adults) returns HTTP 200 with body { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: ISO-8601 string } where count strictly equals flights.length
- GET /search missing any required param (from, to, or date) — including an empty string value — returns HTTP 400 with Content-Type application/json and body { error: string }
- When `adults` is absent on GET /search, the request succeeds (HTTP 200) with a default value of 1 passed to SkyscannerClient
- When `adults` is present but non-numeric (e.g. 'abc', '') on GET /search, the route returns HTTP 400 with Content-Type application/json and body { error: string }
- When `adults` is zero or negative on GET /search, the route returns HTTP 400 with Content-Type application/json and body { error: string }
- When `date` does not match /^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/ on GET /search or GET /cheapest, the route returns HTTP 400 with Content-Type application/json and body { error: string }
- GET /cheapest with valid required params returns HTTP 200 with a single FlightResult whose price is ≤ every FlightResult in the mocked client response; adults defaults to 1 if absent, is forwarded if present
- Adults validation on GET /cheapest is identical to /search: non-numeric or ≤0 returns HTTP 400
- GET /cheapest returns HTTP 404 with Content-Type application/json and body { error: string } when SkyscannerClient returns an empty array
- GET /cheapest missing any required param (from, to, or date) — including empty string — returns HTTP 400 with Content-Type application/json and body { error: string }
- The `searchedAt` field in GET /search is an ISO-8601 datetime string; tests assert `isNaN(new Date(searchedAt).getTime()) === false`
- The FlightResult type in src/server.ts is imported from the SKY-002 export and not redeclared inline
- src/server.test.ts contains at least 8 vitest tests each covering a distinct scenario, with SkyscannerClient mocked via vi.mock so no real HTTP calls are made
- `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0 with no type errors
- `vitest run` exits 0 with all tests passing

